// std — Nessa standard library
//
// The standard library is organized into the following modules:
//
//   std.prelude   — auto-imported symbols (print, println, conversions, etc.)
//   std.io        — input/output primitives
//   std.math      — mathematical functions (abs, sin, cos, sqrt, pow, log, …)
//   std.string    — string operations (str_len, str_concat)
//   std.process   — process control (exit, panic)
//
// Currently all intrinsic functions are registered globally by the compiler.
// Once the module system (`use` statements) is fully implemented, users will
// import from these modules explicitly:
//
//     use std.math.{sin, cos}
//     use std.io.println
//
// The prelude module contents will be auto-imported without an explicit `use`.
